dzn: Compile the indirect-draw and triangle-fan pipelines on first use

dzn_meta_init() compiled a compute pipeline for every indirect-draw
variant and triangle-fan index rewrite the GPU cannot do natively when the
device was created. On a GPU without triangle fans or ExecuteIndirect tier
1.1, such as Intel's Kaby Lake under WSL2, that is 53 pipelines: NIR,
DXIL and a full driver compile each, about a second per vkCreateDevice.
gfxstream creates a Vulkan device for every Android process that draws, so
each app start waited for it, and a boot spent 34 s of CPU on it. Few apps
ever record a draw that needs one of them.

Create each one the first time a command buffer needs it, under a device
lock. A Settings cold start on that GPU went from 2.4 s to 1.5 s.

